Z||000000||Zorba||12-15-2000||05:38 PM||||What the H**L Causes this? Lowe battery juice? Wiper Motor? TUrn signal Switch?<BR>How hard is it to replace the turn signal switch?||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-15-2000||06:03 PM||||Do you have delay wipers?  There was a problem with the wipers wiping a couple times just on start-up for reason at all, caused by a bad delay module.  I dont know if this could be the problem, or just a shorted wire in the turn signal stalk that is giving power to the wipers when it does for the turn signals.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||12-15-2000||10:27 PM||||i have the exact same problem!<BR>not every time, but sometimes, i turn on the key, and the windshield wipers turn on a few times! what the heck!<BR>and it happens sometimes when i use my turn signal.<BR>if you ever figure it out, could you tell me what you did? i'm sure it would be the same thing on my car.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>fiero7@hotmail.com<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||11
